- entry .Base60   the integers 0 to 59, as a union of literal types: a minute or a second
+ entry .Base60   los enteros del 0 al 59, como unión de tipos literales: un minuto o un segundo

= entry .Base60   the integers 0 to 59, as a union of literal types: a minute or a second
-   detail
+   detail

-       `Base60` is the type `0 | 1 | … | 59`, the type of a `Clockface`'s `minute` and
-       `second`, so that `Clockface(14, 30, 59)` typechecks from literals and `Clockface(14,
-       60, 0)` does not. `Base60(int)` wraps an integer modulo 60 (so `Base60(61)` is `1` and
-       `Base60(-1)` is `59`), and `Base60.unapply` matches an `Int` in range, which is how a
-       parsed field becomes one: `(hour, minute, second).absolve match case (Base24(h),
-       Base60(m), Base60(s)) => Clockface(h, m, s)`. The `base60Extractable` given extracts
-       one from text in the same way.
-   entry .apply   an integer reduced modulo 60 to a `Base60`
-   entry .unapply   matches an `Int` between 0 and 59, as a `Base60`
+       `Base60` es el tipo `0 | 1 | … | 59`, el tipo del `minute` y del `second` de un
+       `Clockface`, de modo que `Clockface(14, 30, 59)` comprueba sus tipos a partir de
+       literales y `Clockface(14, 60, 0)` no. `Base60(int)` envuelve un entero módulo 60 (así,
+       `Base60(61)` es `1` y `Base60(-1)` es `59`), y `Base60.unapply` coincide con un `Int`
+       dentro del rango, que es como un campo analizado se convierte en uno: `(hour, minute,
+       second).absolve match case (Base24(h), Base60(m), Base60(s)) => Clockface(h, m, s)`. El
+       given `base60Extractable` extrae uno de un texto de la misma forma.
+   entry .apply   un entero reducido módulo 60 a un `Base60`
+   entry .unapply   coincide con un `Int` entre 0 y 59, como un `Base60`

- entry .Base24   the integers 0 to 23, as a union of literal types: an hour
+ entry .Base24   los enteros del 0 al 23, como unión de tipos literales: una hora

= entry .Base24   the integers 0 to 23, as a union of literal types: an hour
-   detail
+   detail

-       `Base24` is the type `0 | 1 | … | 23`, the type of a `Clockface`'s `hour`. `Base24(int)`
-       wraps an integer modulo 24 (so `Base24(25)` is `1`), and `Base24.unapply` matches an
-       `Int` in range; `base24Extractable` extracts one from text.
-   entry .apply   an integer reduced modulo 24 to a `Base24`
-   entry .unapply   matches an `Int` between 0 and 23, as a `Base24`
+       `Base24` es el tipo `0 | 1 | … | 23`, el tipo del `hour` de un `Clockface`. `Base24(int)`
+       envuelve un entero módulo 24 (así, `Base24(25)` es `1`), y `Base24.unapply` coincide con
+       un `Int` dentro del rango; `base24Extractable` extrae uno de un texto.
+   entry .apply   un entero reducido módulo 24 a un `Base24`
+   entry .unapply   coincide con un `Int` entre 0 y 23, como un `Base24`

- entry .base60Extractable   extracts a `Base60` from text which reads as an integer in range
-     A top-level given: with an `Int` extractor from text in scope, `text match case As[Base60](m)
-     => …` matches text holding an integer from 0 to 59, and `Unset` otherwise. It is imported
-     by name, `import soundness.base60Extractable`, as any top-level given is.
+ entry .base60Extractable   extrae un `Base60` de un texto que se lee como un entero dentro del rango
+     Un given de nivel superior: con un extractor de `Int` a partir de texto en el ámbito,
+     `text match case As[Base60](m) => …` coincide con un texto que contiene un entero del 0 al
+     59, y da `Unset` en otro caso. Se importa por nombre, `import soundness.base60Extractable`,
+     como cualquier given de nivel superior.

- entry .base24Extractable   extracts a `Base24` from text which reads as an integer in range
-     A top-level given, the counterpart of `base60Extractable` for hours: `As[Base24](h)`
-     matches text holding an integer from 0 to 23.
+ entry .base24Extractable   extrae un `Base24` de un texto que se lee como un entero dentro del rango
+     Un given de nivel superior, el equivalente de `base60Extractable` para las horas:
+     `As[Base24](h)` coincide con un texto que contiene un entero del 0 al 23.

- entry .MonthRadix   the radix of some calendar's months, distinct for each calendar
-     A `MonthRadix` is an irregular `Radix` — one whose ratio to the unit below it is not
-     constant — standing for the months of one calendar: `Month` (Gregorian), `IslamicMonth`,
-     `CopticMonth`, `EthiopianMonth`, `HebrewMonth`, `IndianMonth`, `PersianMonth` and
-     `FrenchRepublicanMonth` each extend it. A `Timespan of IslamicMonth.type` is a span counted
-     in Islamic months, which adds only to a date read under the `IslamicCalendar`: adding it
-     under the Gregorian calendar is a compile error, so months of different calendars never
-     mix.
+ entry .MonthRadix   la base de los meses de algún calendario, distinta para cada calendario
+     Un `MonthRadix` es una `Radix` irregular —una cuya razón respecto a la unidad inferior no
+     es constante— que representa los meses de un calendario: `Month` (gregoriano),
+     `IslamicMonth`, `CopticMonth`, `EthiopianMonth`, `HebrewMonth`, `IndianMonth`,
+     `PersianMonth` y `FrenchRepublicanMonth` la extienden. Un `Timespan of IslamicMonth.type`
+     es un lapso contado en meses islámicos, que solo se suma a una fecha leída bajo el
+     `IslamicCalendar`: sumarlo bajo el calendario gregoriano es un error de compilación, de
+     modo que los meses de calendarios distintos nunca se mezclan.

- entry .Week   the radix of weeks: `2*Week` is a `Timespan of Week.type`
+ entry .Week   la base de las semanas: `2*Week` es un `Timespan of Week.type`

= entry .Week   the radix of weeks: `2*Week` is a `Timespan of Week.type`
-   detail
+   detail

-       A regular `Radix` (seven days, always), so `date + 2*Week` needs no policy. `Int is
-       Multiplicable by Week.type` is the given which makes `n*Week` a timespan.
-   entry .multiplicable   `n*Week` as a `Timespan of Week.type`
+       Una `Radix` regular (siete días, siempre), de modo que `date + 2*Week` no necesita
+       política. `Int is Multiplicable by Week.type` es el given que hace de `n*Week` un lapso.
+   entry .multiplicable   `n*Week` como un `Timespan of Week.type`

- entry .Hour   the radix of hours, and the precision marker for `Timestamp in Hour`
+ entry .Hour   la base de las horas, y el marcador de precisión de `Timestamp in Hour`

= entry .Hour   the radix of hours, and the precision marker for `Timestamp in Hour`
-   detail
+   detail

-       `Hour` is both a regular `Radix` object, so that `2*Hour` is a `Timespan of Hour.type`
-       which adds to an `Instant`, a `Timestamp` or a `Moment`, and an erased marker trait, so
-       that `Timestamp in Hour` names an hour-precise timestamp. The `Multiplicable` given is
-       in its companion.
-   entry .multiplicable   `n*Hour` as a `Timespan of Hour.type`
+       `Hour` es a la vez un objeto `Radix` regular, para que `2*Hour` sea un `Timespan of
+       Hour.type` que se suma a un `Instant`, un `Timestamp` o un `Moment`, y un trait marcador
+       borrado, para que `Timestamp in Hour` nombre una marca de tiempo con precisión de hora.
+       El given `Multiplicable` está en su objeto compañero.
