- entry .WeekdayOrdinal   one `BYDAY` entry of a recurrence rule: a weekday, optionally with an ordinal
+ entry .WeekdayOrdinal   una entrada `BYDAY` de una regla de recurrencia: un día de la semana, opcionalmente con un ordinal

= entry .WeekdayOrdinal   one `BYDAY` entry of a recurrence rule: a weekday, optionally with an ordinal
-   detail
+   detail

-       `WeekdayOrdinal(weekday, ordinal = Unset)` is one element of `Rrule#byDay`. A bare weekday
-       (`WeekdayOrdinal(Tue)`, RFC 5545 `TU`) selects every Tuesday in the period; with an
-       ordinal it selects one — `WeekdayOrdinal(Mon, 3)` is the third Monday (`3MO`) and
-       `WeekdayOrdinal(Fri, -1)` the last Friday (`-1FR`), counting back from the end. The
-       ordinal is meaningful only under `Frequency.Monthly` and `Frequency.Yearly`; under
-       `Weekly` and `Daily` a weekday acts as a filter and the ordinal is ignored.
+       `WeekdayOrdinal(weekday, ordinal = Unset)` es un elemento de `Rrule#byDay`. Un día de la
+       semana sin más (`WeekdayOrdinal(Tue)`, `TU` en RFC 5545) selecciona todos los martes del
+       periodo; con un ordinal selecciona uno: `WeekdayOrdinal(Mon, 3)` es el tercer lunes (`3MO`)
+       y `WeekdayOrdinal(Fri, -1)` el último viernes (`-1FR`), contando hacia atrás desde el final.
+       El ordinal solo tiene sentido con `Frequency.Monthly` y `Frequency.Yearly`; con `Weekly` y
+       `Daily`, un día de la semana actúa como filtro y el ordinal se ignora.

