= entry .Weekdays   a choice of weekday names: how a `Weekday` is shown
-   detail
+   detail

-       A `Weekdays` maps each `Weekday` to its name, the context `Weekday.showable` needs and
-       the `Rrule` descriptions use. None is in implicit scope: one is imported by name from the
-       `weekdays` package — `englishWeekdays` (`Monday`), `englishShortWeekdays` (`Mon`),
-       `twoLetterWeekdays` (`Mo`), `oneLetterAmbiguousWeekdays` (`M`, `T`, `W`, `T`, …),
-       `shortestUnambiguousWeekdays` (`M`, `Tu`, `W`, `Th`, …), `frenchWeekdays`,
-       `germanWeekdays` or `spanishWeekdays` — or written as a lambda, since the trait has the
-       single method `#name`.
+       Un `Weekdays` asocia cada `Weekday` a su nombre, el contexto que necesita
+       `Weekday.showable` y que usan las descripciones de `Rrule`. No hay ninguno en el ámbito
+       implícito: se importa uno por nombre del paquete `weekdays` —`englishWeekdays`
+       (`Monday`), `englishShortWeekdays` (`Mon`), `twoLetterWeekdays` (`Mo`),
+       `oneLetterAmbiguousWeekdays` (`M`, `T`, `W`, `T`, …), `shortestUnambiguousWeekdays`
+       (`M`, `Tu`, `W`, `Th`, …), `frenchWeekdays`, `germanWeekdays` o `spanishWeekdays`— o se
+       escribe como una lambda, ya que el trait tiene un único método, `#name`.

=       single method `#name`.
=
